freestanding-lgrt
=================

freestanding-lgrt, the freestanding LLVM and GCC runtime, is an easy to
integrate subset of LLVM's compiler-rt builtins: the libgcc-compatible routines
that GCC and Clang call for operations a target can't do inline, packed into a
single C file.

It covers the integer routines, the atomics, the architecture-specific helpers,
and the functions of C23's stdbit.h.

Supported targets are ELF ones, built with GCC or Clang, for x86-64, IA-32,
aarch64, 32-bit ARM, 32- and 64-bit RISC-V, and 32- and 64-bit LoongArch, plus
16-bit x86 code built with -m16 (GCC, or Clang 12 or later).

To use it, compile src/freestanding-lgrt.c with the same compiler and flags as
the rest of the program, but without LTO (-fno-lto), and link the object in.
The program must provide memcpy, memmove, memset and memcmp. Unsupported
compilers, object formats and architectures stop the build with an error.

Relevant licenses apply: see license headers in source files, LICENSE.TXT and
CREDITS.TXT.
